# TH-Labs Studio — frontend environment.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# You usually do not need to. The committed defaults already point at the real
# backend: `vite dev` proxies /v1 to https://th-labs.uz (see vite.config.ts),
# and `vite build` reads .env.production, which sets the absolute URL. Copy
# this file only to override that — e.g. to develop against a NestJS running on
# your own machine.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_, and it INLINES them at build
# time. Changing any of these in production means rebuilding, not restarting.
#
# Because they are inlined into the JS bundle, everything here is public. Never
# put a payment API key, a JWT secret, or a database URL in this file — those
# belong to the API server only.

# ── Account / billing API (NestJS, Swagger at <host>/docs) ──────────────────
# The CRUD API behind auth, users, payments, health and the language catalog.
# Must include the /v1 suffix.
#
#   local dev     http://localhost:3001/v1
#   production    https://th-labs.uz/v1
#
# ⚠️  https://th-labs.uz/docs is the Swagger UI — a PAGE for humans. It is NOT
#     the API base. Every route it documents lives under /v1, so pointing this
#     at /docs makes each call land on /docs/payments/plans: a 404 with no CORS
#     header, which surfaces in the console as an opaque network failure.
#     Browse /docs, configure /v1. (This file shipped the /docs value for a
#     while — that is the bug, not a hint.)
#
# Leave unset ONLY in local dev, where vite.config.ts proxies /v1 to :3001.
# Unset in a deployed build makes every /v1 call hit the SPA origin and fail.
VITE_ACCOUNT_API=https://th-labs.uz/v1

# ── Dubbing API (FastAPI) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The /jobs pipeline and /media playback ONLY. Include the /api suffix.
#
# health and languages used to be here too, which is why a sleeping GPU box
# took the language picker and the status strip down with it (502 on
# /api/health and /api/languages). Both now come from the account API above —
# see src/lib/api.ts — so this variable only matters once you actually dub.
#
# Unset falls back to the relative /api, which the Vite dev proxy and a
# single-origin reverse proxy both resolve correctly. Against the server box
# that is http://46.224.138.121:8000/api.
VITE_DUB_API=/api

# ── Payments (Lemon Squeezy) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to configure here, on purpose.
#
# Checkout is a Lemon Squeezy share link: GET /v1/payments/checkout returns the
# URL (with the account's email prefilled) and the browser navigates to it, so
# there is no client SDK and no key. Whether payments are configured is
# reported by GET /v1/payments/plans — see LEMONSQUEEZY_* in api/.env.example.
#
# After paying, LS sends the buyer to <this origin>/plans/success, which calls
# POST /v1/payments/claim to credit the order. There is no webhook.

# ── Landing site ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where signing out sends the browser. This app deliberately has no signed-out
# destination of its own: the landing site (th-labs.uz) owns marketing, the
# community signup form and sign-in, and hands a session over with a one-time
# handoff code. So `logout()` clears the session and then leaves for this
# origin — see src/lib/landing.ts.
#
# Optional. Unset, it falls back to https://th-labs.uz, which matches
# `landing_url` in backend/app/config.py.
VITE_LANDING_URL=https://th-labs.uz

# ── Local sign-in (dev only) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Whether a signed-out visitor sees the in-app sign-in screen
# (src/pages/SignIn.tsx) or is redirected to VITE_LANDING_URL.
#
# Leave it unset. It is then ON in `vite dev` and OFF in a production build,
# which is what you want both times: the deployed Studio keeps its single front
# door (the landing site signs you in and hands back a one-time code), while a
# dev server stays reachable. Without it localhost is unusable — it has no
# session, so the gate in AppShell redirects off the origin before any page
# renders.
#
# It only covers ARRIVING without a session. Signing out always leaves for
# VITE_LANDING_URL, in dev as in production.
#
#   true   keep the in-app screen in a non-dev build, e.g. `vite preview`
#   false  restore the landing redirect in dev, to test the real handoff
#
# See src/lib/landing.ts.
# VITE_LOCAL_AUTH=true
